Conservation of Energy Physics Problems,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_DwG8fukuj4,"Works through conservation-of-energy problems involving friction, inclined planes, and springs."
Projectile Motion and Conservation of Energy - College Physics,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DFNTKiOB7t0,Solves projectile-motion problems using both conservation of energy and kinematic equations.
What is a Kilowatt hour?,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4BXZuQyAtIA,"Explains the kilowatt-hour as a unit of energy, converts it to megajoules, and calculates electricity costs for household appliances."
"Dot Product Formula of Power, Force, and Velocity",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WSP07nOjDvo,Explains how to calculate instantaneous power from force and velocity vectors using the dot product.
Conservation of Momentum In Two Dimensions - 2D Elastic & Inelastic Collisions - Physics Problems,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9YRgHikdcqs,Explains two-dimensional momentum conservation by treating the x and y components separately and distinguishes elastic from inelastic collisions.
Impulse and Momentum - Formulas and Equations - College Physics,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FYKoU0sb9ks,"Presents formulas for impulse, momentum, mass flow rate, and one-dimensional elastic and inelastic collisions."
Impulse Formula - Definite Integral - Physics and Calculus,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Zs7N7W8VvbI,Explains how to calculate the impulse of a variable force by integrating the force function over time.
Impulse and Momentum Conservation - Inelastic & Elastic Collisions,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FfaEbqmvKQA,"Reviews impulse, momentum, elastic and inelastic collisions, impulse from force-time graphs, and final velocities from momentum and kinetic-energy conservation."
Center of Mass Physics Problems - Basic Introduction,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2uszSnvzBEU,Explains how to find the center of mass of discrete masses in one and two dimensions and where to place a load to center a truck's mass.
"Rotational Motion Physics, Basic Introduction, Angular Velocity & Tangential Acceleration",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WQ9AH2S8B6Y,"Introduces rotational motion and its relationship to translation, including angular displacement, angular velocity and acceleration, frequency, period, tangential acceleration, and centripetal acceleration."
"Angular Velocity Physics Problems, Linear Speed, Frequency & Period",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=d5VXZGinKSk,"Explains angular and linear velocity, converting between angular speed and linear speed, and calculating angular velocity from frequency and period."
"Angular Acceleration Physics Problems, Radial Acceleration, Linear Velocity",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a99sO7pogXA,"Calculates angular, radial, tangential, and net acceleration in non-uniform circular motion and relates them to linear velocity."
"Rotational Kinematics Physics Problems, Basic Introduction, Equations & Formulas",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0El-DqrCTZM,"Introduces rotational kinematics and solves problems involving angular velocity, angular acceleration, angular displacement, and time."
"Torque, Basic Introduction, Lever Arm, Moment of Force, Simple Machines & Mechanical Advantage",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jg4e8W44_E4,"Introduces torque, lever arms, rotational sign conventions, and the mechanical advantage of simple machines such as seesaws and shovels."
Torque Vs Horsepower Explained - Automotive Car Engines & Physics,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S23AOeGP_Os,"Distinguishes torque from horsepower and calculates torque, horsepower, and engine speed in revolutions per minute."

